$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Run All screen proposed for slice 8,$
# each row's state from the control's real Check, each change$
# the real control's Plan, all of them in one plan on the real$
# plan/apply engine. Which controls hardn.yml asks for, how a$
# row is skipped, and the hostname asked whatever the risk are$
# the gallery's stand-ins, unit (b)'s to build. Nothing on this$
# machine changes: every command and file is the fake's.$
$
# Info: runall/container$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. debian13 in an LXC$
# container: DNS and the firewall are the host's. hardn.yml:$
# george with a key, port 22, two nameservers, backups on, and$
# enableUnattendedUpgrades, enableUfwSshPolicy, configureDns and$
# disableRootSSH true.$
$
# Run All ######################################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured Already as asked$
  [+] Firewall             Configured Already as asked$
  [ ] SSH Login            Partial Root login off$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured Nothing asked$
  [ ] SSH Port             Not Configured Already as asked$
  [-] AppArmor             Not Applicable Status only$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured Already as asked$
  [-] DNS                  Not Applicable container$
  [+] Backups              Configured Used, not changed$
  [ ] Environment          Not Configured Nothing asked$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Apply all            Plan, review, confirm$
                           [ ] Lockout risk$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Apply all ####################################################$
$
# Run All ------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  SSH Login            Root login off$
$
   -  Install hardn's boot unit$
      /etc/systemd/system/hardn-boot.service$
      @@ -0,0 +1,23 @@$
      +# hardn's boot unit (P-34 (c);$
      | docs/safety/revert-boot.md). hardn installs$
      +# it before it arms the revert timer of a change that$
      | could lock you out, and$
      +# removes it at a boot that finds no change journalled.$
      +#$
      +# At boot, before sshd reads its files: re-arm the revert$
      | timer of a change$
      +# waiting for "hardn confirm", for what remains of its$
      | window, or roll the$
      +# change back when its deadline has passed. Ordering$
      | only: sshd starts$
      +# whatever this unit does.$
      +[Unit]$
      +Description=hardn: re-arm or run the revert timer of an$
      | unconfirmed change$
      +DefaultDependencies=no$
      +After=local-fs.target sysinit.target ufw.service$
      +Before=ssh.service ssh.socket shutdown.target$
      +Conflicts=shutdown.target$
      +$
      +[Service]$
      +Type=oneshot$
      +RemainAfterExit=yes$
      +ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/hardn rollback --boot$
      +TimeoutStartSec=7min$
      +$
      +[Install]$
      +WantedBy=multi-user.target$
      -not installed$
      +installed and enabled$
      $ systemd-analyze verify --recursive-errors=no$
      | /run/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx/hardn-boot.service$
      $ systemctl --no-reload enable hardn-boot.service$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Disallow root login$
$
      /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
      @@ -0,0 +1,3 @@$
      +# Managed by hardn.$
      +# Set by hardn:$
      +PermitRootLogin no$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Reload sshd (ssh.service)$
$
      ssh.service$
      $ systemctl reload ssh.service$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      sshd -T shows no root login$
$
      sshd -T$
      $ sshd -T$
$
  Apply this plan?$
$
  Type the hostname [web-01, 0 or q]: web-01$
$
  [+] Install hardn's boot unit    Done$
  [+] Disallow root login          Done$
  [+] Reload sshd (ssh.service)    Done$
  [+] sshd -T shows no root login  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# Warning$
# This change reverts automatically in 3:01$
# To keep it, open a new SSH session and run:$
$
      $ sudo hardn confirm$
$
  Unless confirmed, change 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx is rolled$
  back at 12:03:01 UTC. To undo it now, run sudo hardn rollback$
  20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx.$
$
# Run All ######################################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured Already as asked$
  [+] Firewall             Configured Already as asked$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured Already as asked$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured Nothing asked$
  [ ] SSH Port             Not Configured Already as asked$
  [-] AppArmor             Not Applicable Status only$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured Already as asked$
  [-] DNS                  Not Applicable container$
  [+] Backups              Configured Used, not changed$
  [ ] Environment          Not Configured Nothing asked$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Apply all            Nothing to change$
                           [-] Unavailable$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: runall/container$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Install hardn's boot unit$
      /etc/systemd/system/hardn-boot.service$
      $ systemctl --no-reload enable hardn-boot.service$
$
   -  Armed the revert timer$
      $ systemd-run$
      | --unit=hardn-revert-20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
      | "--description=hardn: roll back change$
      | 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx unless confirmed"$
      | --on-active=180s --timer-property=AccuracySec=1s$
      | /usr/local/bin/hardn rollback 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
   -  Applied: Disallow root login$
      /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
$
   -  Applied: Reload sshd (ssh.service)$
      $ systemctl reload ssh.service$
$

